  "review_text": "# Independent review — nonlocal transmutation audit\n\n- **Reviewed candidate SHA-256:** `3161cd840a02ab5109d6de7d065460e04aa90a5042562fa5471413db0e9d4710`\n- **Primary HTML SHA-256:** `b292563edfd58432859c43f1c835610e65c2414188e0237f69f8c009cf41634d`\n- **Accepted COUPLEDFLUX raw SHA-256:** `258fe6d40ab6b92b4c7a5645fb75ad5dadecd7848a7567e18c0553a65b28b0c4`\n\n**VERDICT: CLEAN_PARTIAL_ANALOGUE_AND_EXACT_NONLOCAL_TRANSFER_ONLY.**\n\n## Direct checks\n\n- The Volterra kernel `(3/2)e^(-X-t)1_(t>=X)` has Hilbert--Schmidt norm squared `9/32`. Direct differentiation gives `[A0,K]=6e^(-2X)`, with the stated orientation, hence `Ltilde T=T diag(A0,A0)` and N2 retains both actual forcing components.\n- N3 has the correct transformed boundary values. The compact-interior test demonstrates that the inverse transform does not preserve a usual zero boundary condition; it does not concern a negative `V` row.\n- N4--N5 exactly retain the physical weighted observation `PZ=Y2`, the coefficient-row dependence, and the `k` derivative. No endpoint was silently discarded.\n- For an actual one-shift source row, gauge covariance gives `Z_k=e^(-2kx)Z_0`; since `x<0`, the unweighted positive auxiliary flux is negative while the physical diagonal `V(x,x)` is positive. This correctly rejects only replacement of the physical energy by that auxiliary metric.\n\nThe cited Theorems 4.1--4.3 in the inspected primary do state a scalar finite-interval transmutation, its inverse, and the resulting intertwining under continuous scalar-potential, nonvanishing-solution, Goursat-kernel hypotheses. The candidate accurately labels it a partial analogue: none of its domain, norm, forcing, or endpoint conclusions applies to the present two-channel half-line block.\n\nThe three query receipts are accurately treated as `INCOMPLETE`, never as no-hit evidence. The candidate makes no theorem, absence, terminal-`V`, or RH claim and correctly stops after the nonlocal expression transfer.\n",
  "verdict": "ACCEPT_EXACT_NONLOCAL_TRANSFER_AND_SCOPED_AUXILIARY_FLUX_OBSTRUCTION_ONLY",
